WEBVTT

00:00.900 --> 00:03.700
Every great athlete, after a big game,

00:03.700 --> 00:06.220
does one thing without fail.

00:06.220 --> 00:08.480
They review the game tape.

00:08.480 --> 00:10.620
They don't just do it to beat themselves up

00:10.620 --> 00:14.800
over their mistakes, they do it to learn.

00:14.800 --> 00:18.220
They watch with their eyes like a coach,

00:18.220 --> 00:20.860
objective and curious.

00:20.860 --> 00:23.940
Your life experiences are your game tape.

00:23.940 --> 00:26.780
The highs, the lows, the turning points,

00:26.780 --> 00:31.080
they all contain powerful data about your passions,

00:31.080 --> 00:33.340
what truly matters to you,

00:33.340 --> 00:36.540
and especially your resilience.

00:36.540 --> 00:40.860
But let's be clear about what resilience means here.

00:40.860 --> 00:43.960
It isn't about how fast you bounce back,

00:43.960 --> 00:48.500
it's about how fully you learn while you're down,

00:48.500 --> 00:53.020
ensuring every comeback is smarter, not just stronger.

00:53.020 --> 00:54.940
In the final drill for this lesson,

00:54.980 --> 00:57.540
we're going to prompt you to review your tape

00:57.540 --> 00:59.540
with that lens.

00:59.540 --> 01:03.180
First, I want you to think about a specific moment

01:03.180 --> 01:08.180
in your career when you felt truly alive and successful,

01:09.020 --> 01:11.160
a peak performance moment.

01:11.160 --> 01:12.820
What was that project?

01:12.820 --> 01:15.620
What was that specific role?

01:15.620 --> 01:18.960
Now, success isn't always a straight line.

01:18.960 --> 01:22.940
Sometimes the most powerful parts of your success formula

01:22.940 --> 01:27.040
are forged in moments that start with a no.

01:28.180 --> 01:31.700
I remember pitching my big idea to executives

01:31.700 --> 01:36.400
at two NFL franchises and getting denied.

01:36.400 --> 01:38.980
I was disappointed, frustrated,

01:38.980 --> 01:42.100
I felt inadequate and a little embarrassed,

01:42.100 --> 01:45.740
but the mental muscle of resilience kicked in

01:45.740 --> 01:48.740
and forged a new belief for me.

01:48.740 --> 01:50.300
I would say this,

01:50.300 --> 01:54.560
I stand on a mountain of nos to get to one yes.

01:55.460 --> 01:59.500
Three years later, I got that yes.

01:59.500 --> 02:03.820
And a once rejected idea became the first ever

02:03.820 --> 02:07.960
player brand university in professional sports.

02:07.960 --> 02:10.820
As you think about your peak performance,

02:10.820 --> 02:13.660
don't just look at the final win,

02:13.660 --> 02:16.660
look at the resilience it took to get there.

02:17.540 --> 02:19.940
That is your success formula.

02:20.700 --> 02:23.380
Then I want you to think about a time

02:23.380 --> 02:27.140
when you faced a significant challenge or setback.

02:27.140 --> 02:31.340
We look back, not with judgment, but with curiosity.

02:32.300 --> 02:34.060
These key plays from your life

02:34.060 --> 02:36.660
contain the final set of clues we need

02:36.660 --> 02:40.260
to build your powerful M.V.P. blueprint.

02:40.260 --> 02:44.100
Resilience reveals what truly matters,

02:44.100 --> 02:48.980
what sustains you and it tests what you've outgrown.

02:48.980 --> 02:51.340
Learning from your past gives you the tools

02:51.340 --> 02:53.700
to lead through what's next.
